          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எனினும் — eṉiṉum — \"nevertheless; however\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மழை பெய்தது, எனினும் போட்டி நடந்தது. maḻai peytatu, eṉiṉum pōṭṭi naṭantatu. It rained. Nevertheless, the match took place."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A formal written word; the everyday one is இருந்தாலும். It opens the second sentence, with a comma."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எனினும் (eṉiṉum) is native: it is eṉ, \"to say\" (DEDR 868), with the concessive ending -இனும், \"even if\": \"even if it is said so\"."
            }
          ]
        },
